# res://dialogue/greene_office.dialogue
# added by Claude (step 2.197): lines for Dr. Greene's office.

~ photo_after_lockscreen
Player: (Oh, isn't this the same lady as on his lock screen?)
Player: (Seems so... He must be really fond of this old-time actress.)
Player: (Huh. Didn't know he had this side to him...)
=> END

~ lockscreen_after_photo
Player: (Oh, isn't this the same lady as in the framed photo?)
Player: (Seems so... He must be really fond of this old-time actress.)
Player: (Huh. Didn't know he had this side to him...)
=> END

~ office_locked_keycard
# step 2.270: first use / examine of dr. greene's office door or its card reader (4F), while locked.
# plays once (greene_office_keycard_talk_seen); sends them to the janitor for a keycard.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
# step 2.377: Layla's expressions (rig). she enters as "base"; this lands while she fades in.
do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
do Flags.set_level_flag("greene_office_keycard_talk_seen", true)
do actor_change("Fiona", "suspicious")
Player: This seems to be locked as well.
Player: Seems like we'll need a keycard to enter, though.
do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
Layla: A keycard?
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
Layla: Wait, didn't the janitor say something about something like that today?
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
Player: (She's right...)
# the janitor again: her face falls (same pose)
do actor_change("Layla", "stern")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Welp. Let's go ask him then.
# a closed-mouth "Ugh" on purpose (puffed cheeks), as at Jayce's "sugars"
do actor_change("Layla", "fuming")
Layla: Ugh. Okay.
do actor_change("Layla", "angry_talk")
Layla: Sorry, I just can't stand him.
do actor_change("Layla", "angry")
Player: Understandable.
=> END

~ office_door
# step 2.280: the door overlay's entry point. right after jayce unlocks the office, the entry talk;
# otherwise the locked-door keycard talk (step 2.270).
if Flags.get_level_flag("greene_office_entry_pending") == true:
	=> office_entry_talk
=> office_locked_keycard

~ office_entry_talk
# step 2.280: first use of the office door after jayce unlocked it. layla waits outside; fiona goes in alone.
# step 2.408: layla keeps following after this talk; the office door sets layla_waiting_outside_office as
# fiona goes in (the level detaches her follower then; the office exit door re-attaches her).
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
do Flags.set_level_flag("greene_office_entry_pending", false)
# step 2.377: Layla's expressions (rig). she enters as "base"; this lands while she fades in.
do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
Layla: He really did open it.
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: I guess we should go in now.
do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
Player: Yes.
# she notices the look (same pose)
do actor_change("Layla", "who_me")
You take a long, hard look at Layla before you enter.
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: You know what?
Player: I think you should stay out here. Let me go in alone.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: ...Why?
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "who_me_talk")
	Layla: Huh? But why?
	do actor_change("Layla", "who_me")
Player: While I totally think the professor and the university won't take any strict actions against ME if we get caught...
Player: I can't say the same for you.
Player: I'm a grad student. You're a fresh undergrad.
Player: It's likely the same rules don't apply to us.
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: But-
do actor_change("Layla", "pensive")
She takes a moment, but what you said seems to have finally gotten through to her.
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: It'll be fine. I'll be in and out in a second.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: If you say so.
	Layla: Fine. I'll wait here.
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
	Layla: You sure?
	do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
	Player: Yes.
	do actor_change("Layla", "admiring")
	Layla: Okay then. I'll wait right here for you.
	do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
Player: Good.
=> END
